The signature: type submit_day_plan = (_: {
day: number,
// The city for this day. If the plan is to travel between two cities, indicate it as "from A to B" (e.g. "from Ithaca to Charlotte").
current_city: string,
// e.g. "Flight Number: F3633413, from Ithaca to Charlotte, Departure Time: 05:38, Arrival Time: 07:46"
transportation: string,
// The name of a restaurant in the city, e.g. "Nagaland's Kitchen, Charlotte"
breakfast: string,
// Use a ";" to separate different attractions, with each attraction formatted as "Name, City". e.g. "The Charlotte Museum of History, Charlotte;"
// e.g. "Cafe Maple Street, Charlotte"
lunch: string,
// e.g. "Bombay Vada Pav, Charlotte"
dinner: string,
// e.g. "Affordable Spacious Refurbished Room in Bushwick!, Charlotte"
accommodation: string,
}) => any;

I see there is no field "city", only "current_city". The description says "city for this day" but actual param is "current_city". So we should use "current_city" to indicate location, and omit city param. So we need to pass day, current_city, transportation, breakfast, attraction, lunch, dinner, accommodation. No "city". Let's adjust.

We need to include travel description? Maybe include in transportation. So current_city will be the city you are in that day (or maybe "Sun Valley" day1). For travel days, you could set current_city as "Sun Valley" or "San Francisco". Good.

Now re-submit day1.

